HitachiTEMTIFF_to_OME-TIFF

Overview
This application converts Hitachi TEM image files (.tif) and their associated metadata files (.txt) into OME-TIFF format. The output is compatible with Fiji, ImageJ, Bio-Formats, and other OME-aware software.

Features
- Graphical user interface
- Batch processing of multiple files
- OME-compliant output
- Metadata mapping for stage, magnification, acquisition time
- Additional metadata preserved as annotations

Requirements
- Java 17 or newer
- Maven (only required for building from source)

Check Java installation:
java -version

Check Maven installation:
mvn -version

Running the Application
Place the .jar file in a folder containing .tif and .txt pairs.

Run by double-clicking the .jar or using:
java -jar hitachi_to_OME-TIFF_converter.jar

The application will:
- Detect valid files
- Ask for confirmation
- Convert all files

Output files are created as:
filename.ome.tif

Building from Source
Navigate to the project root directory and run:
mvn clean package

The compiled JAR will be located at:
target/hitachi_to_OME-TIFF_converter-1.0-shaded.jar

Run the built JAR:
java -jar target/hitachi_to_OME-TIFF_converter-1.0-shaded.jar

Metadata Mapping
Standard OME fields:
- PixelSize → Pixels.PhysicalSizeX/Y
- StagePositionX/Y/Z → Plane.PositionX/Y/Z
- Magnification → Objective.NominalMagnification
- Date and Time → Image.AcquisitionDate

All other metadata is stored as structured annotations.

Notes
- Pixel size is converted from nanometers to micrometers
- Existing .ome.tif files are not overwritten
- Some TEM-specific fields are not defined in OME and are stored as annotations

